 A successful `selectModel` response acknowledges the Session-local selection without waiting for the default profile setting to save. Default saves run in the background in submission order; a failure logs a warning and leaves the Session selection intact. New Sessions read the last successfully saved default.
 
+`selectModelForSession` applies a validated model only to the named Session and never saves the global default. Discover it through `modelCatalog.capabilities.selectModelForSession === true`; older Hosts without the capability are unsupported, and callers must not fall back to `selectModel`. Its `{ selected, scope: 'session', status: 'applied', seq }` response identifies the in-memory `model/selection` event, not a disk durability barrier. A running request keeps its assembled selection; the new selection applies at the next assembly. Recheck the actual request header, since another caller may subsequently select a different model in the same Session.
+
